  abstract:
    "Questionnaires are essential tools in Human-Machine Interaction (HMI)
    research for evaluating human factors. However, two major challenges persist
    in this interdisciplinary field: first, the use of self-constructed and
    non-validated scales, which exacerbates the replication crisis; and second,
    the increasing development of new questionnaires, which makes it difficult
    for researchers to maintain an overview and choose appropriate
    questionnaires. Additionally, existing resources that aim to provide an
    overview of published questionnaires often fall short due to limited
    functionalities, e.g., lacking filtering options, being language-specific,
    missing questionnaires, or no contribution possibilities."
